$\sqrt[16]{5}+1 = 2\cos \frac{\pi}{5^8}$.
Then
$$ x = \frac{4}{ (2\cos \frac{\pi}{5})(2\cos \frac{\pi}{25})(2\cos \frac{\pi}{125})(2\cos \frac{\pi}{625})} = \frac{4}{16 \cos \frac{\pi}{5} \cos \frac{\pi}{25} \cos \frac{\pi}{125} \cos \frac{\pi}{625}} = \frac{1}{4 \cos \frac{\pi}{5} \cos \frac{\pi}{25} \cos \frac{\pi}{125} \cos \frac{\pi}{625}} $$
Let $\theta = \frac{\pi}{625}$. Then $x = \frac{1}{4 \cos \frac{\pi}{5} \cos \frac{\pi}{25} \cos \frac{\pi}{125} \cos \theta}$.
$(x+1)^{48} = \left(\frac{1}{4 \cos \frac{\pi}{5} \cos \frac{\pi}{25} \cos \frac{\pi}{125} \cos \theta} + 1\right)^{48}$

We can rewrite $x$ as $x = \frac{4}{ (\sqrt{5}+1) (\sqrt[4]{5}+1) (\sqrt[8]{5}+1) (\sqrt[16]{5}+1)} $.
