Let $C_{48}$ be the cost of the 48-ounce size and $C_{32}$ be the cost of the 32-ounce size.
We are given that $C_{48} = \$3.90$.
Let $p_{48}$ be the price per ounce for the 48-ounce size.
Then $p_{48} = \frac{C_{48}}{48} = \frac{3.90}{48}$.
Let $p_{32}$ be the price per ounce for the 32-ounce size.
Then $p_{32} = \frac{C_{32}}{32}$.
We are given that the company wants to charge a price per ounce for the smaller size that is 25\% more than the price per ounce for the larger size.
So, $p_{32} \times 1.25 = p_{48}$.
We have $p_{48} = \frac{3.90}{48}$.
So, $p_{32} \times 1.25 = \frac{3.90}{48}$.
