If a function is both even and odd, then we must have $f(-x) = f(x)$ and $f(-x) = -f(x)$.
Therefore, $f(x) = -f(x)$, which implies $2f(x) = 0$, so $f(x) = 0$ for all $x$ in the domain.

Thus, the only function that is both even and odd is the function $f(x) = 0$.

The domain of the function is all real numbers.

The number of such functions is 1.

