Since $a$ is not a multiple of 3, $a \equiv 1 \pmod 3$ or $a \equiv 2 \pmod 3$.
Similarly, since $b$ is not a multiple of 3, $b \equiv 1 \pmod 3$ or $b \equiv 2 \pmod 3$.
