Similarly, $b^2 \equiv 1 \pmod 3$.
Therefore, $a^2 + b^2 \equiv 1 + 1 \equiv 2 \pmod 3$.
Thus, the remainder when $a^2 + b^2$ is divided by 3 is 2.

